  "question": {
    "text": "Pressure inside two soap bubbles are 1.01 and 1.02 atmosphere, respectively. The ratio of their volumes is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "cXT0l",
      "text": "$4: 1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OIi8m",
      "text": "$0.8: 1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vkyDc",
      "text": "$8: 1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "uk1pB",
      "text": "$2: 1$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "According to question, pressure inside, 1st soap bubble,\n$\\Delta P_1=P_1-P_0=0.01=\\frac{4 T}{R_1}$    .....(i)\nAnd $\\Delta P_2=P_2-P_0=0.02=\\frac{4 T}{R_2}$     .....(ii)\nDividing, equation (ii) by (i),\n$\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{R_2}{R_1} \\Rightarrow R_1=2 R_2$\nVolume $V=\\frac{4}{3} \\pi R^3 \\Rightarrow \\frac{V_1}{V_2}=\\frac{R_1^3}{R_2^3}=\\frac{8 R_2^3}{R_2^3}=\\frac{8}{1}$",
    "image": null
  },
